{"name":"Bells and Whistles Gold","hex":"#ede3a1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bells","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of bell"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ship's bells; the strokes on a ship's bell, every half-hour, to mark the passage of time.","Ellipsis of bell-bottoms."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bells"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"whistles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of whistle"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of whistle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistles"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whistle","blocks":[{"text":"A whistle is a musical instrument which produces sound from a stream of gas, most commonly air. The whistle makes a high-pitched, piercing, and shrill sound. It is a type of fipple flute, and may be mouth-operated, or powered by air pressure, steam, or other means. Whistles vary in size from a small slide whistle or nose flute type to a large multi-piped church organ."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Pea_Whistle.jpg/330px-Pea_Whistle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whistle","wikidata":"Q204917"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/V29D_Fixed_Whistle.stl/500px-V29D_Fixed_Whistle.stl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/V29D_Fixed_Whistle.stl/1280px-V29D_Fixed_Whistle.stl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/V29D_Fixed_Whistle.stl/500px-V29D_Fixed_Whistle.stl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 3D-printable whistle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AV29D_Fixed_Whistle.stl"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Party_whistle_on_radio.jpg/500px-Party_whistle_on_radio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1